    {
      "text": "A timeline graphic headed 'Timeline of SPDX Evolution - Use Case by Use Case', with a 'MITRE' logo at the bottom left and the footer '(c) 2024 The MITRE Corporation. All rights reserved. Approved for Public Release; Distribution Unlimited. Case No: 23-01614-54'. A row of blue arrow segments carries years and versions: 2010 'SPDX begins', 2011 'SPDX 1.0', 2013 'SPDX 1.2', 2015 'SPDX 2.0', 2018 '2.1 to ISO', 2019, 2020, 2021 'SPDX 2.3', 2022, 2023 'SPDX 3rc1', 2024+ 'SPDX 3.0'. Below the arrows: 2010 'Standardized Single Package Information: Machine and human readable formats'; 2011 'Compliance Use Cases: Additional Project and License Information'; 2013 'Package Relations: 30+ additional use cases supported for complex packaging relationships and distribution scenarios'; 2015 'Security use cases: External references for vulnerabilities and product identification'; 2020 'SPDX & 3T-SBOM efforts merge: SPDX revises charter as an SDO'; 2021 'Free ISO Standard: ISO/IEC 5962 SPDX available' with a thumbnail of the 'ISO/IEC 5962:2021' cover; 2022 'Format Interoperability' with CDx and SPDX logos; 2023 'Profiles: New areas of use cases: Build, Data, Security, AI, Lite'; 2024+ 'Profiles: New areas of use cases: Services, Hardware, Safety'. Above the arrows: an 'I AM THE Cavalry' logo with 'Legislation: proposed software transparency, updatability & bill of material as reqts in safety critical sectors (automotive & healthcare)'; the NTIA seal with 'NTIA: Software Transparency begins'; OMG and CISQ logos with '3T-SBOM: OMG/CISQ begins w/ CONOPs for Tool-to-Tool SBOM'; two vertical labels 'SPDX 3.0 initial draft' and '3T-SBOM initial draft' at 2020; a seal with 'Transition of SBOM work to DHS'; a thumbnail of 'Executive Order on Improving the Nation's Cybersecurity' with 'Executive Order 14028'; and a document thumbnail with 'EU Cyber Resilience Act'.",
